1
00:03:08,560 --> 00:03:11,000
Are you afraid he'll get into
another accident like today?

2
00:03:11,080 --> 00:03:11,920
Watch out!

3
00:03:13,160 --> 00:03:14,840
Or are you afraid the truth will come out?

4
00:03:14,920 --> 00:03:15,760
PREVIOUSLY

5
00:03:15,840 --> 00:03:17,800
Dad, Nuchwara is pregnant.

6
00:03:17,880 --> 00:03:21,520
You'll claim the baby
as yours instead of Raiwin.

7
00:03:22,160 --> 00:03:23,000
What?

8
00:03:23,080 --> 00:03:26,120
I've told you many times
not to bring that child here.

9
00:03:26,200 --> 00:03:28,360
You don't trust me anymore?

10
00:03:28,440 --> 00:03:32,320
I already told you.
You used up all the trust I had in you.

11
00:03:32,400 --> 00:03:34,520
Did you find any discrepancies?

12
00:03:35,120 --> 00:03:37,480
None of the expenses were inflated.

13
00:04:00,440 --> 00:04:02,000
These are the purchase records

14
00:04:02,520 --> 00:04:04,600
from the end of last year
through this year.

15
00:04:12,000 --> 00:04:16,560
Why would Hathaya lie
to help cover up what Liu did?

16
00:04:39,640 --> 00:04:41,040
I bought this for you.

17
00:04:42,720 --> 00:04:45,320
A little thank-you
for helping me last night.

18
00:04:52,000 --> 00:04:53,200
You don't have to thank me.

19
00:04:54,200 --> 00:04:55,520
It was my responsibility.

20
00:04:56,040 --> 00:04:59,120
I wasn't about to let a house
I built burn down.

21
00:05:00,440 --> 00:05:03,640
But it wasn't your responsibility
to stop by so late at night.

22
00:05:04,440 --> 00:05:05,720
Why did you really go there?

23
00:05:07,000 --> 00:05:08,000
I…

24
00:05:08,920 --> 00:05:11,200
-I forgot something.
-Max told me everything.

25
00:05:13,000 --> 00:05:15,200
You were bringing me some bedding.

26
00:05:18,680 --> 00:05:20,120
Thank you.

27
00:05:24,040 --> 00:05:25,520
But you won't have to go

28
00:05:27,760 --> 00:05:30,000
out of your way for me anymore.

29
00:05:36,080 --> 00:05:38,840
Today is the last day of the month

30
00:05:39,600 --> 00:05:42,320
I promised Grandpa I'd work for him.

31
00:05:46,480 --> 00:05:51,120
I'm going to collect the rest
of my money and go home.

32
00:05:57,520 --> 00:05:58,480
And…

33
00:06:03,600 --> 00:06:05,000
are you ever coming back?

34
00:06:07,840 --> 00:06:10,960
You know they don't want me here.

35
00:06:13,600 --> 00:06:15,400
I'm going to use this money

36
00:06:16,920 --> 00:06:18,240
for Grandma's treatment…

37
00:06:20,680 --> 00:06:22,000
and take care of her.

38
00:06:26,200 --> 00:06:28,280
I'm not coming back here again.

39
00:06:33,480 --> 00:06:35,400
Thank you

40
00:06:36,640 --> 00:06:38,840
for always helping me.

41
00:06:43,480 --> 00:06:45,000
You're a good person.

42
00:06:47,040 --> 00:06:50,200
One of the best people I've ever met.

43
00:06:54,200 --> 00:06:56,360
If I could ask one thing of you…

44
00:07:00,080 --> 00:07:02,400
Don't keep your feelings…

45
00:07:05,000 --> 00:07:06,960
and your kindness hidden all the time.

46
00:07:10,520 --> 00:07:12,440
Stop taking your anger out
on your own life.

47
00:07:14,040 --> 00:07:15,960
It doesn't make anything better.

48
00:07:17,640 --> 00:07:19,760
It only makes things worse.

49
00:07:23,720 --> 00:07:25,680
I'm going back to pack my things.

50
00:07:26,840 --> 00:07:29,320
Tomorrow morning…

51
00:07:33,120 --> 00:07:34,240
I'll leave.

52
00:07:39,560 --> 00:07:40,920
Goodbye.

53
00:08:22,040 --> 00:08:24,560
I've completed the full month
of work we agreed on.

54
00:08:25,600 --> 00:08:27,880
I came to collect the final payment.

55
00:08:27,960 --> 00:08:29,880
Then I'm going home.

56
00:08:35,320 --> 00:08:37,799
Your wages, as promised.

57
00:08:55,000 --> 00:08:59,720
So you're going home?
Your husband isn't trying to stop you?

58
00:09:04,680 --> 00:09:06,840
I want to say this one last time.

59
00:09:07,560 --> 00:09:11,200
What happened between Ramil and me
was a misunderstanding.

60
00:09:12,200 --> 00:09:15,280
There's no reason for us
to keep living together.

61
00:09:16,000 --> 00:09:18,800
Have a safe trip, Hathaya.

62
00:09:20,360 --> 00:09:22,200
I probably won't be able to see you off.

63
00:09:22,800 --> 00:09:25,640
I have so much work to help Grandpa with.

64
00:09:28,400 --> 00:09:31,400
Grandpa, before I go,

65
00:09:32,120 --> 00:09:34,800
may I go upstairs and pay
my respects to Dad's ashes?

66
00:09:36,520 --> 00:09:38,320
You should go home.

67
00:09:38,400 --> 00:09:39,400
Please.

68
00:09:39,480 --> 00:09:41,600
Your family has probably
been waiting for you.

69
00:10:14,840 --> 00:10:16,560
You can go now.

70
00:10:53,560 --> 00:10:54,640
She's gone.

71
00:10:55,160 --> 00:10:57,520
I hope she never sets foot here again.

72
00:10:59,320 --> 00:11:03,480
I'm so satisfied. Father
wouldn't even acknowledge her farewell.

73
00:11:04,000 --> 00:11:05,960
He still hates her.

74
00:11:54,160 --> 00:11:56,120
I let your daughter go home.

75
00:11:57,800 --> 00:11:59,640
Not because I don't love my granddaughter.

76
00:12:05,840 --> 00:12:09,200
But because I don't want
anyone hurting her anymore.

77
00:12:16,240 --> 00:12:18,280
And I want Hathaya

78
00:12:19,000 --> 00:12:21,000
to go back and take care
of the people she loves.

79
00:12:50,800 --> 00:12:52,520
-Hello.
-Hello.

80
00:12:54,880 --> 00:12:55,840
Where's Hathaya?

81
00:12:55,920 --> 00:12:58,720
Oh, Miss Hathaya
already left for the bus station.

82
00:13:00,320 --> 00:13:02,240
Mr. Pichai is waiting for you
in his office.

83
00:13:03,240 --> 00:13:04,120
Okay.

84
00:13:34,000 --> 00:13:38,720
DUANGJAI'S FOOD STALL

85
00:13:44,960 --> 00:13:46,880
Order whatever you want.

86
00:13:46,960 --> 00:13:48,760
Anything is fine.

87
00:13:48,840 --> 00:13:52,040
I heard Grandma Duangjai
makes everything delicious.

88
00:13:52,840 --> 00:13:54,400
Hathaya!

89
00:13:54,480 --> 00:13:56,120
You're back?

90
00:13:58,080 --> 00:13:59,600
I missed you so much.

91
00:14:03,640 --> 00:14:04,480
Grandma.

92
00:14:04,560 --> 00:14:06,200
-Yes?
-Grandma.

93
00:14:06,280 --> 00:14:07,480
-Yes, sweetheart?
-It's burning.

94
00:14:07,560 --> 00:14:08,400
Everything's burning.

95
00:14:08,480 --> 00:14:10,880
Your food is burning.

96
00:14:10,960 --> 00:14:12,480
I forgot.

97
00:14:12,560 --> 00:14:14,200
How do you live alone like this?

98
00:14:15,040 --> 00:14:15,960
This isn't good.

99
00:14:16,040 --> 00:14:18,280
-What if the stall catches fire?
-I'll cook it again.

100
00:14:18,360 --> 00:14:19,920
You can't cook the stall again

101
00:14:20,000 --> 00:14:22,720
if the whole thing burns down.

102
00:14:24,720 --> 00:14:26,280
I missed you so much.

103
00:14:26,360 --> 00:14:28,320
Why are you so thin?

104
00:14:29,160 --> 00:14:30,920
How have you been?

105
00:14:31,000 --> 00:14:34,920
Have you been taking your medicine?
Are you still getting dizzy?

106
00:14:36,000 --> 00:14:38,400
I'm old.

107
00:14:38,480 --> 00:14:41,400
Some mornings I wake up
and the whole room spins.

108
00:14:43,120 --> 00:14:44,840
Old? You're beautiful.

109
00:14:46,600 --> 00:14:50,760
Grandma, I went to work for Grandpa.
He paid me.

110
00:14:50,840 --> 00:14:51,760
Here.

111
00:14:52,280 --> 00:14:55,120
This money is for your treatment.
It's yours. Take it.

112
00:14:55,200 --> 00:14:58,280
No. I'm still strong.

113
00:14:58,360 --> 00:15:00,320
You need to keep some money for yourself.

114
00:15:01,200 --> 00:15:02,080
I don't care.

115
00:15:02,160 --> 00:15:05,040
I worked for this money specifically
so I could give it to you.

116
00:15:05,120 --> 00:15:08,160
You have to take it. It's yours.

117
00:15:09,600 --> 00:15:11,280
All right.

118
00:15:11,360 --> 00:15:13,600
But I'll keep it for you.

119
00:15:16,560 --> 00:15:20,280
My Grandma Duangjai is
the most stubborn person in the world.

120
00:15:25,400 --> 00:15:26,560
Where's Mom?

121
00:15:32,520 --> 00:15:33,600
Grandma.

122
00:15:34,360 --> 00:15:38,640
What has Mom been doing? Where is she?

123
00:15:38,720 --> 00:15:40,120
Is she okay?

124
00:15:40,960 --> 00:15:42,400
I don't want to talk about her.

125
00:15:44,760 --> 00:15:48,680
You two fight every day.

126
00:15:49,280 --> 00:15:51,520
What was it this time?

127
00:15:52,760 --> 00:15:54,240
I've cut her out of my life.

128
00:15:56,400 --> 00:15:58,920
Grandma, why?

129
00:15:59,440 --> 00:16:01,240
What did Mom do?

130
00:16:01,760 --> 00:16:04,200
Tell me everything.

131
00:16:07,240 --> 00:16:09,280
Why didn't you use that money
to pay your debt?

132
00:16:09,360 --> 00:16:11,320
I gambled it all away.

133
00:16:15,640 --> 00:16:17,040
Call Hathaya.

134
00:16:17,120 --> 00:16:19,920
Tell her you're in the hospital
and need emergency surgery.

135
00:16:20,000 --> 00:16:22,240
Tell her to send money.

136
00:16:22,320 --> 00:16:25,000
I'll use it to pay those people.

137
00:16:25,080 --> 00:16:29,040
The girl told me everything about the kind
of work you were recruiting her for.

138
00:16:29,800 --> 00:16:32,360
I don't want you doing anything illegal.

139
00:16:32,440 --> 00:16:34,120
Find something else to do.

140
00:16:36,520 --> 00:16:38,120
NOW HIRING: FEMALE SERVERS AND HOSTESSES

141
00:16:47,240 --> 00:16:48,600
Well, hello there.

142
00:16:51,080 --> 00:16:52,240
You look good.

143
00:16:53,080 --> 00:16:54,120
Here to apply for work?

144
00:16:54,800 --> 00:16:56,360
Come on. I'll take you inside.

145
00:16:56,960 --> 00:16:58,200
Don't touch me.

146
00:16:58,280 --> 00:16:59,760
What a pain.

147
00:17:00,560 --> 00:17:01,840
If you don't want a job, get out.

148
00:17:02,840 --> 00:17:05,000
I'm not here to apply.

149
00:17:09,000 --> 00:17:10,319
What are you doing here?

150
00:17:11,000 --> 00:17:13,800
I'm looking for my mother.
Her name is Hathai.

151
00:17:15,680 --> 00:17:18,200
I'm your mother's husband.

152
00:17:19,640 --> 00:17:21,720
Hello. You're Big, right?

153
00:17:22,319 --> 00:17:24,960
Hathai talks about you a lot.

154
00:17:25,040 --> 00:17:26,880
You're even prettier than your mother.

155
00:17:28,040 --> 00:17:31,000
She's inside. I'll take you to her.

156
00:17:33,880 --> 00:17:34,800
Come on.

157
00:17:45,360 --> 00:17:49,120
Hathai took a girl out to a customer.

158
00:17:49,200 --> 00:17:50,040
There it is.

159
00:17:50,800 --> 00:17:52,640
Big is something else.

160
00:17:52,720 --> 00:17:54,880
He's had the mother,
and now he wants the daughter too.

161
00:18:06,280 --> 00:18:07,520
Where's my mother?

162
00:18:08,640 --> 00:18:11,160
She's working in one of the rooms.
I'll take you.

163
00:18:11,240 --> 00:18:13,200
I can wait here.

164
00:18:13,280 --> 00:18:15,080
It's too loud here.

165
00:18:15,160 --> 00:18:17,680
A mother and daughter
need somewhere private to talk.

166
00:18:17,760 --> 00:18:20,400
Hathai has been saying
she wants to see you. Come on.

167
00:18:46,000 --> 00:18:47,040
Where's my mother?

168
00:18:47,640 --> 00:18:49,360
I thought she was here.

169
00:18:50,000 --> 00:18:51,760
She must've gone
to take care of a customer.

170
00:18:52,800 --> 00:18:53,960
Hey.

171
00:18:54,680 --> 00:18:57,360
Sit down and wait.
I'll get you something to drink.

172
00:18:58,000 --> 00:19:01,000
No. If my mother isn't here,
I'm going home.

173
00:19:01,080 --> 00:19:03,520
Tell her I'm back home now.

174
00:19:04,840 --> 00:19:05,880
Are you scared of me?

175
00:19:07,040 --> 00:19:10,040
I'm not scared. I just don't trust you.

176
00:19:10,120 --> 00:19:12,240
We just met.

177
00:19:12,320 --> 00:19:14,800
Why are you so cynical?

178
00:19:16,880 --> 00:19:18,760
A decent person wouldn't run a brothel.

179
00:19:21,600 --> 00:19:22,600
Let me go.

180
00:19:22,680 --> 00:19:25,480
Let me go. Help! Let me go.

181
00:19:30,760 --> 00:19:32,160
In two hours,

182
00:19:32,240 --> 00:19:35,200
-go pick Joy up from the hotel.
-Yes.

183
00:19:36,160 --> 00:19:37,160
Thank you.

184
00:19:39,560 --> 00:19:41,440
Who's my husband fooling around with?

185
00:19:44,560 --> 00:19:45,640
Gip?

186
00:19:47,640 --> 00:19:49,800
-Then who?
-Your daughter.

187
00:19:53,080 --> 00:19:54,040
Big.

188
00:19:56,680 --> 00:19:59,000
Help. Let me go! Help!

189
00:19:59,080 --> 00:20:02,240
-Help. Help!
-You can scream. No one is coming to help.

190
00:20:02,320 --> 00:20:04,080
Help! No!

191
00:20:04,160 --> 00:20:05,520
Let me go! Let me go!

192
00:20:05,600 --> 00:20:07,120
Mom, help me.

193
00:20:13,760 --> 00:20:14,840
The hell are you doing to my girl?

194
00:20:14,920 --> 00:20:16,160
Nothing.

195
00:20:16,240 --> 00:20:19,400
I was just teaching her the job.
She can help us make money.

196
00:20:23,520 --> 00:20:27,200
I don't care who else you go after,
but stay away from my daughter.

197
00:20:27,280 --> 00:20:30,400
Then get her out of here. Fine,
I don't want her. You've ruined the mood.

198
00:20:41,480 --> 00:20:42,560
Mom, let's go.

199
00:20:44,160 --> 00:20:45,000
You…

200
00:20:53,520 --> 00:20:55,240
Where did Hathaya go?

201
00:20:55,320 --> 00:20:57,360
She said she was going to see a friend.

202
00:20:57,440 --> 00:20:59,480
Why isn't she back yet?

203
00:21:02,480 --> 00:21:04,880
Hathaya. Where were you?

204
00:21:05,880 --> 00:21:08,520
She came to see me.

205
00:21:09,560 --> 00:21:10,600
I told you

206
00:21:10,680 --> 00:21:13,240
not to go to places like that.

207
00:21:13,320 --> 00:21:15,160
Don't get involved with bad people.

208
00:21:15,240 --> 00:21:16,720
You're so stubborn.

209
00:21:17,360 --> 00:21:18,880
What happened to you?

210
00:21:22,480 --> 00:21:24,560
Mom's new husband tried to rape me.

211
00:21:26,960 --> 00:21:28,960
You overreacted.

212
00:21:29,040 --> 00:21:31,080
He knew you were my daughter.

213
00:21:31,160 --> 00:21:33,600
He was just fooling around.

214
00:21:34,560 --> 00:21:35,600
Mom.

215
00:21:36,400 --> 00:21:38,960
Your husband took off his clothes
and tried to rape me,

216
00:21:39,040 --> 00:21:40,800
and you still think it's no big deal?

217
00:21:41,400 --> 00:21:43,320
He didn't actually do anything to you.

218
00:21:43,400 --> 00:21:44,760
Stop making such a fuss.

219
00:21:44,840 --> 00:21:46,040
Hathai.

220
00:21:46,560 --> 00:21:48,040
You let your husband

221
00:21:48,120 --> 00:21:49,640
try to rape your own daughter.

222
00:21:49,720 --> 00:21:52,680
I don't even know what insults
are bad enough for you anymore.

223
00:21:53,400 --> 00:21:54,680
Your husband does something evil

224
00:21:54,760 --> 00:21:56,400
and you still defend him?

225
00:21:56,480 --> 00:21:58,960
I already yelled at him, Mom.

226
00:22:00,400 --> 00:22:02,520
And I got her out of there

227
00:22:02,600 --> 00:22:04,160
and brought her home.

228
00:22:04,800 --> 00:22:08,240
Honestly, you're the one to blame.

229
00:22:08,320 --> 00:22:10,040
You let her come looking for me there.

230
00:22:10,120 --> 00:22:12,240
If she hadn't,
none of this would've happened.

231
00:22:12,320 --> 00:22:14,760
Oh, I see. So I'm wrong.

232
00:22:14,840 --> 00:22:17,480
Your daughter is wrong,
and the brothel is blameless?

233
00:22:17,560 --> 00:22:19,160
Fine.

234
00:22:19,240 --> 00:22:22,600
Hathaya, call the police. Tell them
to raid that brothel right now.

235
00:22:22,680 --> 00:22:24,520
Have them arrest every last one of them.

236
00:22:24,600 --> 00:22:25,640
Mom.

237
00:22:26,240 --> 00:22:29,000
You just want money, don't you?
Is that why you're threatening me?

238
00:22:31,600 --> 00:22:32,800
Here.

239
00:22:32,880 --> 00:22:34,520
Take it. And stop threatening me.

240
00:22:34,600 --> 00:22:36,480
I wouldn't take anything from you.

241
00:22:36,560 --> 00:22:38,040
Fine. Then don't.

242
00:22:38,120 --> 00:22:40,640
And if you get sick,
don't come asking me for help.

243
00:22:40,720 --> 00:22:42,240
I'm not taking you to the hospital.

244
00:22:42,320 --> 00:22:44,280
Even if I die, don't come to my funeral.

245
00:22:44,360 --> 00:22:47,120
Throw her out.
I don't want to see her face.

246
00:22:51,400 --> 00:22:52,440
Mom.

247
00:22:56,040 --> 00:22:58,480
Close the place down
and leave your new husband.

248
00:23:00,920 --> 00:23:01,920
I'm not leaving him.

249
00:23:03,120 --> 00:23:06,640
The reason I have money and
live comfortably now is because of him.

250
00:23:06,720 --> 00:23:09,760
Are you going to wait
until the police arrest you?

251
00:23:09,840 --> 00:23:12,160
My husband has powerful connections.

252
00:23:12,240 --> 00:23:14,040
Who's going to arrest him?

253
00:23:14,120 --> 00:23:15,920
Stay out of my business.

254
00:23:16,000 --> 00:23:18,360
How can I stay out of it?

255
00:23:18,440 --> 00:23:22,760
Every time you mess up,
Grandma and I clean up your mess.

256
00:23:22,840 --> 00:23:24,000
Oh.

257
00:23:24,080 --> 00:23:27,800
Holding your favors over my head?
Ungrateful brat!

258
00:23:27,880 --> 00:23:30,320
You went to live with Grandpa,
in a rich family,

259
00:23:30,400 --> 00:23:31,880
living comfortably.

260
00:23:31,960 --> 00:23:33,920
You have no idea how hard
I've had to struggle.

261
00:23:34,000 --> 00:23:35,560
And do you have any idea

262
00:23:35,640 --> 00:23:37,920
what I went through there?

263
00:23:38,880 --> 00:23:41,320
No one ever welcomed me.

264
00:23:42,160 --> 00:23:45,200
They despised me
because I'm your daughter.

265
00:23:49,520 --> 00:23:52,480
Everyone there branded me
as being just like you.

266
00:23:53,600 --> 00:23:56,720
They kept humiliating me
and treating me badly.

267
00:23:58,080 --> 00:24:02,120
I put up with all of it because I wanted
to earn money to pay off your debt.

268
00:24:03,600 --> 00:24:05,920
But you gambled it all away.

269
00:24:07,960 --> 00:24:12,480
I let them push me around
just to pay for Grandma's treatment.

270
00:24:15,320 --> 00:24:17,680
And I wanted them to see

271
00:24:18,560 --> 00:24:20,080
that I'm not like you.

272
00:24:23,280 --> 00:24:24,160
Hey.

273
00:24:24,720 --> 00:24:27,680
Don't start talking to me
like some high-class lady.

274
00:24:29,720 --> 00:24:32,160
I have to support myself.

275
00:24:32,680 --> 00:24:34,360
I have to survive.

276
00:24:34,440 --> 00:24:36,120
Yes, Mom.

277
00:24:36,920 --> 00:24:40,000
Everyone has to struggle to survive.

278
00:24:40,520 --> 00:24:45,160
But there has to be a better way.
You have to choose something legal.

279
00:24:45,760 --> 00:24:46,600
Look.

280
00:24:46,680 --> 00:24:48,400
I'm your mother.

281
00:24:48,480 --> 00:24:51,800
You don't get to lecture me.
You're the one who should listen to me.

282
00:24:51,880 --> 00:24:53,800
Enough, Hathai.

283
00:24:53,880 --> 00:24:56,840
If you still can't tell right from wrong,

284
00:24:56,920 --> 00:24:59,480
you have no business
lecturing anyone. Go away.

285
00:24:59,560 --> 00:25:01,480
Get out of my house. Right now.

286
00:25:01,560 --> 00:25:04,080
Fine. I don't want to stay anyway.

287
00:25:04,160 --> 00:25:05,920
It's better if we all live our own lives.

288
00:25:08,240 --> 00:25:10,640
And let me tell you something, Mom.

289
00:25:10,720 --> 00:25:15,040
Everything I do
is for you and my daughter.

290
00:25:15,120 --> 00:25:17,400
I want all of you to live comfortably.

291
00:25:18,000 --> 00:25:20,880
But if no one appreciates me,

292
00:25:22,840 --> 00:25:24,280
then I don't care.

293
00:25:35,440 --> 00:25:37,160
Hathaya…

294
00:25:41,320 --> 00:25:42,960
My dear.

295
00:26:06,160 --> 00:26:11,080
DUANGJAI'S FOOD STALL

296
00:26:12,480 --> 00:26:13,760
Grandma.

297
00:26:15,040 --> 00:26:17,240
When is Mom ever going to realize

298
00:26:18,200 --> 00:26:20,000
what she's doing and feel sorry for it?

299
00:26:20,720 --> 00:26:22,360
I'm sorry.

300
00:26:22,440 --> 00:26:26,080
I must not have raised her well.
That's why she turned out this way.

301
00:26:27,080 --> 00:26:28,240
Hathaya.

302
00:26:29,280 --> 00:26:33,520
I had no idea you were suffering
so much over there.

303
00:26:34,600 --> 00:26:38,160
Why didn't you tell me the truth,

304
00:26:38,240 --> 00:26:39,840
that they didn't want you there?

305
00:26:41,840 --> 00:26:44,520
Because I was worried about you and Mom.

306
00:26:46,600 --> 00:26:48,720
I didn't want either of you
worrying about me.

307
00:26:50,320 --> 00:26:51,880
I love you so much, Grandma.

308
00:26:57,960 --> 00:27:00,560
Let all the bad things stay in the past.

309
00:27:01,080 --> 00:27:03,160
Let the bad people leave our lives.

310
00:27:05,040 --> 00:27:08,280
And we'll start over. Okay, sweetheart?

311
00:27:11,320 --> 00:27:12,240
Yes, Grandma.

312
00:27:16,400 --> 00:27:18,640
We'll start a new life.

313
00:27:20,240 --> 00:27:22,560
We won't be parasites
living off anyone anymore.

314
00:27:42,520 --> 00:27:45,160
DUANGJAI'S FOOD STALL

315
00:27:45,240 --> 00:27:46,720
Here you go.

316
00:27:46,800 --> 00:27:49,160
One delicious railroad fried rice.

317
00:27:49,240 --> 00:27:52,040
The spoons and forks are right here.
And here's the best part.

318
00:27:52,120 --> 00:27:54,920
This chili fish sauce is really good.

319
00:27:55,000 --> 00:27:57,800
But I'm warning you, just have a little
or your tummy might regret it.

320
00:28:01,920 --> 00:28:04,400
I haven't seen her
this happy in a long time.

321
00:28:08,920 --> 00:28:11,480
Who's that young man spying on Hathaya?

322
00:28:16,600 --> 00:28:17,720
Hey, young man.

323
00:28:18,480 --> 00:28:19,680
What are you doing?

324
00:28:23,560 --> 00:28:24,720
I…

325
00:28:25,680 --> 00:28:28,120
You what? What are you thinking,

326
00:28:28,640 --> 00:28:31,760
snooping on my granddaughter?
Show your face.

327
00:28:32,800 --> 00:28:33,680
Hey.

328
00:28:35,120 --> 00:28:36,000
Hey, young man.

329
00:28:36,520 --> 00:28:39,080
Don't run away. Come back here.

330
00:28:40,320 --> 00:28:41,520
What's with him?

331
00:28:42,040 --> 00:28:42,960
Grandma.

332
00:28:43,480 --> 00:28:44,920
What happened?

333
00:28:46,040 --> 00:28:47,200
Here, let me carry those.

334
00:28:47,280 --> 00:28:49,600
Some guy was spying on you.

335
00:28:50,360 --> 00:28:51,680
When I tried to see his face,

336
00:28:52,280 --> 00:28:53,840
he took off like a rocket.

337
00:28:55,160 --> 00:28:56,800
Who was it?

338
00:28:56,880 --> 00:29:01,120
I don't know. Come to think of it,
he did look kind of familiar.

339
00:29:02,920 --> 00:29:04,720
You'll have to get used to it.

340
00:29:04,800 --> 00:29:07,880
When you have a beautiful granddaughter,
men are going to look.

341
00:29:09,640 --> 00:29:12,880
Maybe he was looking at me.

342
00:29:14,400 --> 00:29:15,640
Wow, the hottest woman on the block.

343
00:29:15,720 --> 00:29:18,920
Grandma, you're the prettiest woman
on this whole street.

344
00:29:19,000 --> 00:29:20,440
Of course I am.

345
00:29:22,040 --> 00:29:23,160
But no thanks.

346
00:29:23,240 --> 00:29:26,440
Children wear you out,
and husbands give you headaches.

347
00:29:26,520 --> 00:29:27,920
I don't want either. Come on.

348
00:29:28,000 --> 00:29:29,720
I bought plenty of groceries.

349
00:29:29,800 --> 00:29:31,240
I'll carry them. Come on.

350
00:29:31,320 --> 00:29:34,560
You're so tiny and skinny,
and men still come looking for you.

351
00:29:42,760 --> 00:29:43,840
That was close.

352
00:29:54,520 --> 00:29:55,360
Mr. Pichai.

353
00:29:58,920 --> 00:29:59,760
Yes, sir.

354
00:29:59,840 --> 00:30:01,280
How is Hathaya?

355
00:30:01,360 --> 00:30:03,160
She's helping her grandma
at the food stall.

356
00:30:03,760 --> 00:30:07,360
From what I can see, she seems happy.

357
00:30:07,440 --> 00:30:09,200
And Hathaya's mother?

358
00:30:09,280 --> 00:30:10,600
I haven't seen her.

359
00:30:11,320 --> 00:30:13,640
I was going to ask
some people around here.

360
00:30:13,720 --> 00:30:15,800
Please look into it for me.

361
00:30:17,080 --> 00:30:21,440
I want to make sure she won't cause any
more trouble for Hathaya or her grandma.

362
00:30:22,040 --> 00:30:22,880
Yes, sir.

363
00:30:29,840 --> 00:30:30,800
Excuse me.

364
00:30:31,560 --> 00:30:35,560
Do you know where Hathaya's mother is now?
She used to work at the food stall.

365
00:30:35,640 --> 00:30:38,200
Do you know what she's doing for work?

366
00:30:38,280 --> 00:30:39,720
Oh…

367
00:30:46,840 --> 00:30:50,080
If you want to know about my mother,
you can ask me.

368
00:31:05,240 --> 00:31:08,560
Were you following me?

369
00:31:08,640 --> 00:31:12,680
I think I should be asking you that.
You were spying on me earlier.

370
00:31:13,240 --> 00:31:15,480
How did you know?

371
00:31:21,920 --> 00:31:24,560
Because I actually saw you spying on me.

372
00:31:35,200 --> 00:31:36,160
You really are…

373
00:31:36,840 --> 00:31:38,280
sharp.

374
00:31:41,200 --> 00:31:42,880
Thanks for the compliment.

375
00:31:43,440 --> 00:31:46,840
But you still haven't answered me.
What are you investigating?

376
00:31:50,120 --> 00:31:52,640
Well… I…

377
00:31:52,720 --> 00:31:53,760
And don't lie.

378
00:31:58,840 --> 00:32:01,040
Mr. Pichai sent me.

379
00:32:03,080 --> 00:32:04,240
Grandpa?

380
00:32:04,320 --> 00:32:05,440
-Yes.
-Really?

381
00:32:06,920 --> 00:32:10,640
Mr. Pichai asked me to find out
what your mother is doing

382
00:32:10,720 --> 00:32:13,440
and whether she's still bothering you.

383
00:32:14,720 --> 00:32:16,080
He's really worried about you.

384
00:32:21,040 --> 00:32:22,160
Then,

385
00:32:23,160 --> 00:32:24,760
please tell Grandpa

386
00:32:25,360 --> 00:32:29,080
he doesn't need to worry anymore.
My mother is working somewhere else.

387
00:32:29,600 --> 00:32:32,400
No one is bothering Grandma or me now.

388
00:32:34,000 --> 00:32:36,600
Yes, ma'am. I'll report back.

389
00:32:48,560 --> 00:32:51,120
Your job here is done. You can go now.

390
00:32:52,040 --> 00:32:53,320
Wow.

391
00:32:54,080 --> 00:32:56,440
You see me and immediately kick me out?

392
00:32:57,400 --> 00:32:59,080
I'm worried about Papang.

393
00:32:59,600 --> 00:33:02,640
If he's not with you,
he's probably being really difficult.

394
00:33:08,480 --> 00:33:09,920
Max is watching him.

395
00:33:10,000 --> 00:33:11,440
It's not the same.

396
00:33:12,480 --> 00:33:13,720
You should go back.

397
00:33:20,360 --> 00:33:21,600
All right.

398
00:33:23,320 --> 00:33:25,680
I'm glad to see you and your grandmother

399
00:33:27,040 --> 00:33:27,920
happy.

400
00:33:29,440 --> 00:33:31,520
I'm happy for you and your new life.

401
00:33:33,440 --> 00:33:34,920
I hope you're happy from now on.

402
00:33:43,240 --> 00:33:44,080
That's it?

403
00:34:03,520 --> 00:34:04,800
Father.

404
00:34:04,880 --> 00:34:06,560
Who were you talking to?

405
00:34:07,160 --> 00:34:08,159
Ramil.

406
00:34:09,199 --> 00:34:11,520
Was it about the development?

407
00:34:12,880 --> 00:34:17,120
No. I asked Ramil to stop by and check
on Hathaya at her home in the countryside.

408
00:34:22,320 --> 00:34:23,719
Father,

409
00:34:24,239 --> 00:34:25,880
I brought you some ginseng.

410
00:34:25,960 --> 00:34:30,360
Chayanee and I
simmered it for you ourselves.

411
00:34:30,440 --> 00:34:31,840
I'll serve it for you, Grandpa.

412
00:34:33,120 --> 00:34:34,560
No need.

413
00:34:35,239 --> 00:34:38,480
I already drink a tonic every day.

414
00:34:40,560 --> 00:34:42,480
Who makes it for you?

415
00:34:43,880 --> 00:34:48,600
Before Hathaya left,
she bought the herbs and asked the maid

416
00:34:49,120 --> 00:34:50,520
to prepare them for me every day.

417
00:34:51,560 --> 00:34:54,440
Go on. If you have
something to do, go do it.

418
00:34:54,520 --> 00:34:55,840
I'm going to rest.

419
00:34:57,880 --> 00:34:58,840
All right.

420
00:35:00,520 --> 00:35:01,680
Let's go.

421
00:35:25,480 --> 00:35:28,560
I got up early to simmer that for Grandpa,

422
00:35:32,520 --> 00:35:34,320
and he didn't appreciate it at all.

423
00:35:49,160 --> 00:35:50,280
Be patient, sweetheart.

424
00:35:51,960 --> 00:35:53,120
Patient?

425
00:35:54,760 --> 00:35:56,520
How much longer do I have to be patient?

426
00:35:58,120 --> 00:36:01,200
Hathaya isn't even here,
and she's still haunting me.

427
00:36:03,680 --> 00:36:05,920
Does Grandpa love her?

428
00:36:06,440 --> 00:36:08,240
Does he want her to come back?

429
00:36:10,200 --> 00:36:11,480
No.

430
00:36:12,000 --> 00:36:14,720
Older people can be sensitive like this.

431
00:36:14,800 --> 00:36:18,760
Grandpa is still upset. That's why
he keeps comparing you to Hathaya.

432
00:36:21,720 --> 00:36:23,560
You have to be patient.

433
00:36:24,240 --> 00:36:27,400
Keep taking good care of Grandpa.
Before long,

434
00:36:27,480 --> 00:36:29,560
he'll love you the way he used to.

435
00:36:33,040 --> 00:36:33,960
Okay.

436
00:36:36,920 --> 00:36:38,720
I'll be good enough

437
00:36:39,440 --> 00:36:41,400
to make Grandpa forget Hathaya.

438
00:37:11,200 --> 00:37:12,400
What happened?

439
00:37:13,280 --> 00:37:15,120
Let's get to the karaoke club.

440
00:37:26,440 --> 00:37:28,080
The police are raiding the place.

441
00:37:28,680 --> 00:37:30,120
Must be something illegal.

442
00:37:31,120 --> 00:37:34,400
My mother and her new husband
run a brothel.

443
00:37:35,000 --> 00:37:35,920
Huh?

444
00:37:41,360 --> 00:37:42,400
Stop.

445
00:37:42,480 --> 00:37:44,120
Nobody move. Police. Sit down.

446
00:37:44,200 --> 00:37:46,960
Everyone, sit down. Sit down.

447
00:37:47,040 --> 00:37:48,280
Sit down. Sit down.

448
00:37:48,360 --> 00:37:49,840
Stay where you are.

449
00:37:49,920 --> 00:37:51,360
Everyone, listen to me, please.

450
00:37:51,440 --> 00:37:53,360
We need everyone to gather over here.

451
00:37:53,440 --> 00:37:55,280
Don't panic.

452
00:37:55,360 --> 00:37:58,320
Please sit together over here.

453
00:37:58,400 --> 00:38:00,320
Sit down. Just a routine inspection.

454
00:38:00,400 --> 00:38:03,480
We just need to check
everyone's identification. Sit together.

455
00:38:03,560 --> 00:38:04,600
Everyone, listen.

456
00:38:04,680 --> 00:38:06,600
We're going to ask all of you
to come to the station.

457
00:38:06,680 --> 00:38:09,240
Come on.

458
00:38:09,320 --> 00:38:11,560
-Get in the car.
-You bragged about connections.

459
00:38:11,640 --> 00:38:13,360
How did the police raid this place then?

460
00:38:13,440 --> 00:38:15,720
Someone turned against us
to claim the credit.

461
00:38:19,280 --> 00:38:21,680
Come on.

462
00:38:21,760 --> 00:38:23,520
Go over there.

463
00:38:23,600 --> 00:38:26,160
Go on.

464
00:38:26,240 --> 00:38:28,280
I don't see Mom or her new husband.

465
00:38:29,680 --> 00:38:32,120
Maybe they already escaped.

466
00:38:33,920 --> 00:38:36,440
Let's go home. I'm worried about Grandma.

467
00:38:37,960 --> 00:38:40,440
What do we do now?

468
00:38:40,520 --> 00:38:42,160
We run.

469
00:38:46,480 --> 00:38:47,320
Come on.

470
00:38:49,840 --> 00:38:50,760
Stop.

471
00:38:53,240 --> 00:38:54,560
Big!

472
00:38:54,640 --> 00:38:57,080
Did you just kill a cop?

473
00:38:57,160 --> 00:38:58,240
Yeah.

474
00:38:58,320 --> 00:39:01,200
If you don't want to die too, move.

475
00:39:18,840 --> 00:39:22,240
I'm still strong. I'm not sick anymore.

476
00:39:23,200 --> 00:39:25,920
I'm going to keep this money
for you, Hathaya.

477
00:39:38,120 --> 00:39:39,120
What?

478
00:39:39,200 --> 00:39:42,120
Hathaya? Are you home?

479
00:39:43,840 --> 00:39:45,560
Mom. Quick.

480
00:39:45,640 --> 00:39:47,480
-Get inside. Come on.
-What is going on?

481
00:39:47,560 --> 00:39:50,240
-What is going on?
-Just get inside.

482
00:39:50,320 --> 00:39:51,240
Get inside.

483
00:39:51,320 --> 00:39:52,960
Why are you two here?

484
00:39:53,040 --> 00:39:54,360
Keep your voice down.

485
00:39:54,440 --> 00:39:56,520
The police raided the brothel. We escaped.

486
00:39:56,600 --> 00:39:58,720
People as rotten as you deserve it.

487
00:39:58,800 --> 00:40:00,640
Shut up, old woman,

488
00:40:00,720 --> 00:40:03,160
or I'll shoot you
just like I shot that cop.

489
00:40:03,760 --> 00:40:06,520
Then run wherever you want.
Why are you dragging me into this?

490
00:40:07,280 --> 00:40:09,320
The police are right behind us.

491
00:40:09,400 --> 00:40:11,600
We can go out through the back,

492
00:40:11,680 --> 00:40:14,720
cross the road, and lose them. Come on.

493
00:40:15,440 --> 00:40:16,840
You're coming too. Move.

494
00:40:16,920 --> 00:40:18,440
Wait. Stop.

495
00:40:18,520 --> 00:40:20,280
Don't take Mom. Let her go.

496
00:40:20,360 --> 00:40:22,440
We'll take her as a hostage.

497
00:40:22,520 --> 00:40:24,320
That way, we'll lose the police. Move.

498
00:40:24,400 --> 00:40:27,680
-No. Let her go.
-I'm not going.

499
00:40:28,520 --> 00:40:30,560
Wait, Mom. What's in that envelope?

500
00:40:30,640 --> 00:40:31,680
Nothing.

501
00:40:31,760 --> 00:40:33,320
Let me see.

502
00:40:33,400 --> 00:40:34,440
-Let me see.
-It's nothing.

503
00:40:34,520 --> 00:40:35,400
-Let's see.
-Give it.

504
00:40:35,480 --> 00:40:37,000
Let me see.

505
00:40:41,920 --> 00:40:43,760
-Money.
-You can't take that.

506
00:40:43,840 --> 00:40:44,800
It belongs to Hathaya.

507
00:40:44,880 --> 00:40:46,880
I'm keeping it for her.

508
00:40:46,960 --> 00:40:49,240
Mom, let me borrow it.
I'll pay it back later.

509
00:40:49,320 --> 00:40:51,200
-Come on. Move.
-No.

510
00:40:51,280 --> 00:40:53,960
-I'm not going.
-Quickly. Move.

511
00:40:54,040 --> 00:40:57,600
DUANGJAI'S FOOD STALL

512
00:40:58,360 --> 00:41:00,440
Grandma? Grandma?

513
00:41:01,840 --> 00:41:04,360
I have a bad feeling about this.

514
00:41:05,720 --> 00:41:09,240
There are police everywhere out front.
Maybe they went out the back.

515
00:41:10,880 --> 00:41:11,840
Come on.

516
00:41:13,480 --> 00:41:16,040
Move. Hurry.

517
00:41:19,880 --> 00:41:21,000
We'll go this way.

518
00:41:22,480 --> 00:41:24,040
Come on.

519
00:41:25,000 --> 00:41:26,800
-Grandma.
-Grandma.

520
00:41:27,840 --> 00:41:28,720
Grandma.

521
00:41:30,320 --> 00:41:32,600
-Grandma.
-Grandma.

522
00:41:32,680 --> 00:41:35,320
Grandma. Grandma.

523
00:41:36,360 --> 00:41:37,600
Grandma.

524
00:41:37,680 --> 00:41:39,760
Grandma. Where are you?

525
00:41:42,480 --> 00:41:43,760
Grandma.

526
00:41:45,520 --> 00:41:46,360
Hey.

527
00:41:48,360 --> 00:41:49,400
This looks familiar.

528
00:41:51,840 --> 00:41:53,960
That's Grandma's bracelet.

529
00:42:03,200 --> 00:42:05,240
If you're going to run, then run.
Let me go.

530
00:42:21,360 --> 00:42:22,400
Quiet.

531
00:42:33,840 --> 00:42:35,120
Come on. We have a car.

532
00:42:35,200 --> 00:42:36,200
Move.

533
00:42:37,120 --> 00:42:39,600
We have the car. Let Mom go.

534
00:42:39,680 --> 00:42:41,320
Let's just get out of here. Come on.

535
00:42:41,400 --> 00:42:42,400
Yeah.

536
00:42:45,240 --> 00:42:46,160
Hey! What are you doing?

537
00:42:46,240 --> 00:42:48,480
This old woman reported us to the police.

538
00:42:48,560 --> 00:42:50,720
I didn't report you.

539
00:42:50,800 --> 00:42:52,400
But if I'd known how rotten you were,

540
00:42:52,480 --> 00:42:54,040
I would've called the police that day.

541
00:42:54,120 --> 00:42:55,520
Still running your mouth?

542
00:42:55,600 --> 00:42:57,160
She's my mother. Stop.

543
00:42:57,240 --> 00:42:58,400
-Let go.
-Put your gun down.

544
00:42:58,480 --> 00:42:59,920
-Let go.
-I told you not to hurt her.

545
00:43:00,000 --> 00:43:01,800
Grandma! Grandma.

546
00:43:01,880 --> 00:43:03,200
-Hathaya.
-Grandma.

547
00:43:03,280 --> 00:43:04,440
-Come on.
-Hathaya.

548
00:43:04,520 --> 00:43:06,000
Help me.

549
00:43:11,360 --> 00:43:12,880
-Mom.
-Give me the money back.

550
00:43:12,960 --> 00:43:14,320
Give it back.

551
00:43:14,400 --> 00:43:16,560
I told you. I just need
to borrow it to recover.

552
00:43:16,640 --> 00:43:18,040
I don't believe you anymore.

553
00:43:18,120 --> 00:43:20,240
You've already taken
enough money from Hathaya.

554
00:43:20,840 --> 00:43:21,840
Mom.

555
00:43:21,920 --> 00:43:23,800
-I'm not giving it to you.
-Give it back.

556
00:43:23,880 --> 00:43:27,760
-Fine. If you want it, take it.
-Give it back.

557
00:43:29,600 --> 00:43:30,720
Come on. Drive.

558
00:43:30,800 --> 00:43:31,800
I'm not leaving.

559
00:43:32,920 --> 00:43:34,000
Grandma.

560
00:43:35,360 --> 00:43:36,640
Hathaya.

561
00:43:36,720 --> 00:43:38,840
-Grandma. Grandma.
-Grandma.

562
00:43:38,920 --> 00:43:40,760
-Grandma.
-Careful!

563
00:43:42,600 --> 00:43:44,600
Let me go. Grandma. Grandma.

564
00:43:45,520 --> 00:43:46,480
Let me go. Grandma.

565
00:43:46,560 --> 00:43:48,720
-Don't.
-Grandma.

566
00:43:49,360 --> 00:43:50,640
Let me go.

567
00:43:51,520 --> 00:43:52,440
Grandma.

568
00:43:52,520 --> 00:43:53,760
-Grandma.
-Grandma.

569
00:43:54,600 --> 00:43:55,800
Old woman. Come back here.

570
00:43:59,080 --> 00:44:00,920
Let me go.

571
00:44:01,000 --> 00:44:02,040
-Grandma.
-Hathaya!

572
00:44:05,320 --> 00:44:06,360
Grandma.

573
00:44:07,160 --> 00:44:08,400
Grandma.

574
00:44:09,880 --> 00:44:10,880
Hey, old woman.

575
00:44:19,880 --> 00:44:21,800
I said come back!

576
00:44:30,560 --> 00:44:31,640
I said come back.

577
00:44:33,520 --> 00:44:34,880
Quickly.

578
00:44:36,360 --> 00:44:38,840
Grandma. Grandma.

579
00:44:39,520 --> 00:44:41,640
Stop, old woman. Hey!

580
00:44:55,840 --> 00:44:57,000
Grandma!

581
00:45:07,080 --> 00:45:08,520
Mom!

582
00:45:14,520 --> 00:45:17,640
Grandma. Grandma.

583
00:45:25,080 --> 00:45:26,560
Mom!

584
00:45:28,280 --> 00:45:29,120
Grandma.

585
00:45:32,120 --> 00:45:33,640
-Mom.
-Move, quickly.

586
00:45:33,720 --> 00:45:36,440
Come on. Do you want to get arrested?

587
00:45:37,040 --> 00:45:38,440
I said go. Go!

588
00:45:38,520 --> 00:45:39,360
Hey!

589
00:45:40,720 --> 00:45:42,680
Grandma. Let me go.

590
00:45:43,280 --> 00:45:44,280
Mom…

591
00:45:47,600 --> 00:45:49,200
-Grandma.
-Grandma.

592
00:45:49,920 --> 00:45:52,000
Grandma. Grandma.

593
00:45:54,560 --> 00:45:55,840
-Grandma.
-Grandma.

594
00:45:57,200 --> 00:45:58,720
-Grandma, please.
-Grandma.

595
00:45:58,800 --> 00:46:00,720
Help me…

596
00:46:03,040 --> 00:46:03,880
Hello.

597
00:46:04,400 --> 00:46:07,040
Someone's been shot. Please hurry.

598
00:46:11,160 --> 00:46:12,720
Grandma…

599
00:46:15,440 --> 00:46:17,560
What do I do?

600
00:46:18,440 --> 00:46:19,560
Grandma.

601
00:46:21,080 --> 00:46:22,680
Grandma.

602
00:46:39,120 --> 00:46:41,280
RAMIL

603
00:46:49,680 --> 00:46:50,640
Hello?

604
00:46:52,360 --> 00:46:54,120
Why are you calling this late?

605
00:46:55,040 --> 00:46:56,040
What happened?

606
00:46:59,920 --> 00:47:00,880
Huh?

607
00:47:09,720 --> 00:47:10,800
What did the doctor say?

608
00:47:10,880 --> 00:47:13,160
-The doctor still hasn't treated Grandma.
-What?

609
00:47:14,840 --> 00:47:16,440
She's been here for a long time.

610
00:47:21,680 --> 00:47:23,280
How are you?

611
00:47:23,800 --> 00:47:25,400
-I'm coughing.
-Coughing?

612
00:47:25,480 --> 00:47:27,520
Take them inside.

613
00:47:27,600 --> 00:47:29,400
Nurse. Nurse.

614
00:47:29,480 --> 00:47:31,480
-Has the doctor arrived yet?
-Yes.

615
00:47:31,560 --> 00:47:34,480
Then why hasn't the doctor
treated my grandmother?

616
00:47:34,560 --> 00:47:37,320
She's elderly, and she was
seriously wounded by a gunshot.

617
00:47:37,400 --> 00:47:38,680
Are they going to wait until she…

618
00:47:38,760 --> 00:47:41,440
I understand. We're doing
everything we can.

619
00:47:41,520 --> 00:47:44,080
Right now, your grandmother's
vital signs are still stable.

620
00:47:44,160 --> 00:47:45,440
You're doing everything you can?

621
00:47:46,240 --> 00:47:47,840
Then why are patients still waiting?

622
00:47:47,920 --> 00:47:50,680
Look around. There are
so many people here.

623
00:47:50,760 --> 00:47:52,080
Why isn't a doctor treating them?

624
00:47:52,160 --> 00:47:53,400
Please listen.

625
00:47:53,480 --> 00:47:56,800
This is a small hospital near the border.

626
00:47:56,880 --> 00:47:59,480
A lot of patients
cross over for treatment,

627
00:47:59,560 --> 00:48:01,240
and we only have a few doctors.

628
00:48:01,320 --> 00:48:05,720
She hasn't been treated yet
because more critical cases take priority.

629
00:48:06,280 --> 00:48:07,120
Excuse me.

630
00:48:08,240 --> 00:48:10,240
-Wait.
-Ramil.

631
00:48:11,200 --> 00:48:14,320
The doctors and nurses
are doing everything they can.

632
00:48:15,160 --> 00:48:18,040
But what about Grandma?

633
00:48:18,120 --> 00:48:20,000
We have to transfer her
to a private hospital.

634
00:48:20,920 --> 00:48:22,280
I can't.

635
00:48:22,360 --> 00:48:25,280
I don't have the money.
My mother stole all of it.

636
00:48:25,360 --> 00:48:27,120
It's okay. Use my money.

637
00:48:27,720 --> 00:48:30,560
No. I don't want to burden you anymore.

638
00:48:30,640 --> 00:48:32,400
And you need that money too.

639
00:48:33,000 --> 00:48:34,440
For your grandma, I'm willing.

640
00:48:35,040 --> 00:48:37,120
I've already asked too much of you.

641
00:48:37,200 --> 00:48:40,680
And the nurse said
Grandma's vital signs are still stable.

642
00:48:41,360 --> 00:48:42,760
Once they finish with the others,

643
00:48:43,400 --> 00:48:45,680
they'll probably come
treat her. It's okay.

644
00:48:48,520 --> 00:48:51,120
Hathaya. Where are you going?

645
00:48:51,960 --> 00:48:55,400
May the sacred spirits
and guardian deities

646
00:48:55,480 --> 00:48:57,480
of this place

647
00:48:57,560 --> 00:48:59,320
protect my grandmother

648
00:48:59,400 --> 00:49:02,240
and keep her safe.

649
00:49:02,840 --> 00:49:05,600
Grandpa, thank you so much.

650
00:49:05,680 --> 00:49:07,520
NEXT EPISODE

651
00:49:08,080 --> 00:49:08,920
Why did you come back?

652
00:49:09,000 --> 00:49:12,800
I want Hathaya to come back to work
because I need someone honest.

653
00:49:13,400 --> 00:49:14,480
Not people who steal from me like you.

654
00:49:16,120 --> 00:49:17,360
Your father

655
00:49:17,440 --> 00:49:19,040
doesn't want to take care of you.

656
00:49:19,120 --> 00:49:22,760
He wants you to live with your mother.
He wants you out of his life.

657
00:51:17,120 --> 00:51:19,040
Subtitle translation by: Thanit Puncharoen
